diff --git a/docs/agent-hub.md b/docs/agent-hub.md
index 0502c732ee..cc30b240d7 100644
--- a/docs/agent-hub.md
+++ b/docs/agent-hub.md
@@ -87,6 +87,10 @@ While subagents run, a pinned `Subagents` block above the editor lists every liv
 
 The list stays short: it shows a few rows plus an expander (`display.pinnedAgents: collapsed`, the default), lists everything (`full`), or hides entirely (`off`). Clicking the expander toggles between the two while `tui.mouse` is on.
 
+Directly above it, a pinned `Background tasks` block lists the other work running in the background: backgrounded `bash` commands, backgrounded `eval` cells and services. A row shows the task id (`bg_1099`, or the service name), a one-line preview of its command and the elapsed time, right-aligned. Jobs that only run a subagent (every `task` job, including work-pool batches and security scans) are not listed there, since the `Subagents` block and the Hub already show that work. The block appears while something runs, clears itself when nothing does, and repaints its elapsed times once a second only while it is showing.
+
+`display.pinnedJobs` sets its density the same way: `collapsed` (the default) shows a few rows plus an expander, `full` lists everything and `off` hides the block. Clicking its expander toggles between the two while `tui.mouse` is on, and changing the setting resets that click.
+
 Each row ends with that agent's total tokens and API cost, for example `1.4M tok · $0.42`, right-aligned and dim. Tokens count everything the model processed, cache reads included, so the figure matches what the provider counts; the Hub's own `tok` figure leaves cache reads out. Cost appears once it is above zero, because a subscription or unpriced model reports zero and `$0.00` would read as free. A row too narrow to keep a readable title drops the usage and keeps the title.
 
 Set `display.subagentLivePreview: true` to add a second line under each row showing what that agent is doing: its current tool call (or, between calls, the most recent one) with a one-line detail, plus the elapsed time once a call runs longer than five seconds. Off by default.
